## Summary

Audited main at 0259e29 for structural simplification and completed one focused cleanup of Admin queue reporting.

Before: queues.go returned a slice mixing model-derived counts with live thumbnail-attempt counts. dashboard.go cached that slice by model, cloned it, and repaired the entry named "thumbnails" on each snapshot. Dashboard and queue API duplicated live-status assembly.
Now: modelQueues holds named model-derived counts, while Model.queueReport assembles both responses with live thumbnail, search-processing and pending-write status. Queue order and JSON fields are preserved. The cache remains useful without display-name-dependent repair.

Existing queue tests consume the shared report; no new checks, flags, test seams, schema or production-data changes. App-specific redirects and image inheritance were deliberately left separate because their policies differ.

Full internal/db tests passed under timeout 30; go vet ./... and git diff --check passed. At merge preparation, the requested git merge --no-ff --no-commit main reported already up to date; no conflicts or further changes were needed. Tests and vet passed again.

